      "updated": 1793804227951,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Recursion ( Divide and Conquer )\n==============================\n\nDefining something in terms of itself .\n\nIn Programming\n-------------------\n\n1. In programming recursion is used with methods .\n\n2. If a method constains its own call in its own body then we call it a RECURSIVE METHOD .\n\n3. IT is an alternative to looping .\n\n4. Means recursion is used when we want something repeatedly .\n\n5. Every Recusion method must have a base condition in its body .\nThis condition will control recursive call .\n\n\n\nHow java Handles method calls\n===========================\n\npublic class Example3 {\n    public static void goodMorning(int n){\n        System.out.println(\"Good Morning !\");\n    }\n\n    public static void gooAfternoon(){\n        int x=10;\n        goodMorning(x);\n        System.out.println(\"Good Afternoon !\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        int x=10;\n        gooAfternoon();\n        System.out.println(\"Good Night !\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Recursion ( Divide and Conquer )\n==============================\n\nDefining something in terms of itself .\n\nIn Programming\n-------------------\n\n1. In programming recursion is used with methods .\n\n2. If a method constains its own call in its own body then we call it a RECURSIVE METHOD .\n\n3. IT is an alternative to looping .\n\n4. Means recursion is used when we want something repeatedly .\n\n5. Every Recusion method must have a base condition in its body .\nThis condition will control recursive call .\n\n\n\nHow java Handles method calls\n===========================\n\npublic class Example3 {\n    public static void goodMorning(int n){\n        System.out.println(\"Good Morning !\");\n    }\n\n    public static void gooAfternoon(){\n        int x=10;\n        goodMorning(x);\n        System.out.println(\"Good Afternoon !\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        int x=10;\n        gooAfternoon();\n        System.out.println(\"Good Night !\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
